Here is the full **testsmells.org 19-smell academic audit** of `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`.

> **Framework:** MSTest 4.1.0 / .NET 10
> **Integration calibration applied:** Class is tagged `[TestCategory("Integration")]` — Mystery Guest and Eager Test severity are downgraded per the academic calibration rules. Sleepy Test remains high even for integration tests.

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 3 | 3 |
| Medium | 1 | 1 |
| Low | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **4** | **4** |

4 of 8 test methods are clean — acknowledged below.

---

## Findings by Severity

### ❌ HIGH 1 — Conditional Test Logic (testsmells.org: *Conditional Test Logic*)

**Affected:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)
**Risk:** The `if/else` branch means one assertion path *never* executes per run. If the production type hierarchy changes, the untested branch silently rots.

```csharp
// CURRENT — smell
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix:** Split into two tests with deterministic setup, each asserting one code path:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com")!;

    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

---

### ❌ HIGH 2 — Sleepy Test (testsmells.org: *Sleepy Test*)

**Affected:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)
**Risk:** `Thread.Sleep(3000)` adds 3 seconds of wall-clock time per run and is non-deterministic — on a slow CI agent the delay may be insufficient, causing flaky failures. Also, `Thread.Sleep` blocks the thread inside an `async Task` method, which is an additional code smell (async method with synchronous blocking).

```csharp
// CURRENT — smell
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix:** Poll with a timeout instead of sleeping:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll with back-off instead of a fixed sleep
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(5);
    while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        if (_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
            break;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }

    Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
}
```

---

### ❌ HIGH 3 — Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (testsmells.org: *Unknown Test*)

**Affected:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)
**Risk:** This test inserts 100 rows but never asserts anything. MSTest will report it as *passing* even if every insert silently fails (e.g., rows aren't committed). The method name implies a "does-not-throw" intent, but that is implicit — any future regression that corrupts data without throwing will go undetected.

```csharp
// CURRENT — smell
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
{
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
// ← no assertion
```

**Fix:** Assert the observable outcome:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

---

### ⚠️ MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette (testsmells.org: *Assertion Roulette*)

**Affected:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)
**Risk:** 4 assertions with no message parameters. When one fails, the MSTest runner reports the line number, but the failure summary gives no semantic context (e.g., "was it the name, email, or ID that was wrong?").

```csharp
// CURRENT — smell (4 bare assertions)
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix:** Add message parameters:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive");
```

---

## Smells Scanned and Not Found (15 of 19 clean)

| Smell (academic name) | Result | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean | In-memory SQLite (`Data Source=:memory:`) is hermetic; integration-calibrated |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean | Max 3 distinct production methods per test (below 4 threshold); integration-calibrated |
